{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"infinitequeryobserver","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InfiniteQueryObserver"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InfiniteQueryObserver"},{"type":"text","value":" can be used to observe and switch between infinite queries."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const observer = new InfiniteQueryObserver(queryClient, {\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\n  queryFn: fetchPosts,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => lastPage.nextCursor,\n  getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => firstPage.prevCursor,\n})\n\nconst unsubscribe = observer.subscribe((result) => {\n  console.log(result)\n  unsubscribe()\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The options for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InfiniteQueryObserver"},{"type":"text","value":" are exactly the same as those of "},{"type":"link","href":"../../framework/react/reference/useInfiniteQuery","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useInfiniteQuery"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"infinitequeryobserver","text":"InfiniteQueryObserver","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## `InfiniteQueryObserver`\n\nThe `InfiniteQueryObserver` can be used to observe and switch between infinite queries.\n\n```tsx\nconst observer = new InfiniteQueryObserver(queryClient, {\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\n  queryFn: fetchPosts,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => lastPage.nextCursor,\n  getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => firstPage.prevCursor,\n})\n\nconst unsubscribe = observer.subscribe((result) => {\n  console.log(result)\n  unsubscribe()\n})\n```\n\n**Options**\n\nThe options for the `InfiniteQueryObserver` are exactly the same as those of [`useInfiniteQuery`](../../framework/react/reference/useInfiniteQuery).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: InfiniteQueryObserver\ntitle: InfiniteQueryObserver\n---\n\n## `InfiniteQueryObserver`\n\nThe `InfiniteQueryObserver` can be used to observe and switch between infinite queries.\n\n```tsx\nconst observer = new InfiniteQueryObserver(queryClient, {\n  queryKey: ['posts'],\n  queryFn: fetchPosts,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => lastPage.nextCursor,\n  getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => firstPage.prevCursor,\n})\n\nconst unsubscribe = observer.subscribe((result) => {\n  console.log(result)\n  unsubscribe()\n})\n```\n\n**Options**\n\nThe options for the `InfiniteQueryObserver` are exactly the same as those of [`useInfiniteQuery`](../../framework/react/reference/useInfiniteQuery).\n"}
